hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7844","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me Al-Misri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Imran, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah Al-Jamali, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him He said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he sent him to Yemen: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Finish your religion, and your work will suffice for you.” “This is a small hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7844 - Incorrect"
"7845","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Bamru, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Abdullah bin Saeed told us Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Two blessings that are unjustified.” Many people: health and free time “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7845 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"7846","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Abi Hind informed, about... His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man while he was advising him: “Take advantage of five before Five: your youth before your old age, your health before your illness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your work, and your life before Your death “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7846 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7847","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told me, Saeed ibn Sulaiman Al-Wasiti Sa’dawiya told me, Zakaria ibn Manzur told me. Ibn Tha'labah Ibn Abi Malik, Abu Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Sa'd, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a Then he saw a sheep with one leg strayed and said: “Do you think this sheep is easy for its owner?” They said: Yes. He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, this world is easier for God than this for its owner, even if the world were equal to God.” “The wing of a mosquito does not give an unbeliever a drink of water from it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7847 - Zakaria bin Manzur is weak"
"7848","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khalid bin Khadash bin Ajlan Al-Muhallabi told us, Abd told us Allah bin Wahb, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him He said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was feverish, so I put my hand on top of the velvet and felt the heat of his fever and said: How intense your fever is, O Messenger of God. He said: “We are like that, community of prophets. The pain will be doubled for us so that the reward will be doubled for us.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, that is. People are more afflicted? He said: “The Prophets.” I said: Then who? He said: “Then are the righteous. If a man is afflicted with poverty until he finds nothing but a cloak, he covers it and wears it, and if one of them He will be plagued with lice until the lice kills him, and that is more beloved to them than giving to you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7848 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7849","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told us, saying: Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Saleh told us. Al-Wahazi, Abu Ismail Al-Sakouni told us, he said: I heard Malik bin Adi saying: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, saying, and he On the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, nothing remains of the world except the likes of flies passing through its atmosphere. By God “God bless your brothers among the people of the graves, for your deeds will be presented to them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7849 - It contains two unknowns"
"7850","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told me, Baqiya bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The heart of the son of Adam is like a bird, turning over seven times a day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7850 - There is an interruption"
"7851","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Abu Aqeel told us Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yazid bin Sinan, on the authority of Bukair bin Fayrouz, saying: He heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Whoever is afraid will go in, and whoever goes in will have reached the final destination. Indeed, God’s goodness is precious. Indeed, God’s goodness is precious.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7851 - True"
"7852","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fears He entered and whoever entered has reached the final destination. Indeed, God’s commodity is precious. Verily, God’s commodity is Paradise, the trembling one has come, followed by the equivalent one, it has come. “Death and all that is in it”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7852 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7853","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bukayr, Al-Adl, told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab Al-Sha’arani told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Amr bin Abi Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves his world will be harmed by his hereafter, and whoever loves his hereafter will be harmed by his worldly life, so choose what “It endures as it perishes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7853 - There is a break"
"7854","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b. Ibn Ujrah, on the authority of Zainab bint Kaab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. A man said: O Messenger of God, have you seen these diseases that It afflicts us, what do we do with it? He said: “Atonements.” Ubayy bin Ka’b said: O Messenger of God, even if it is small? He said: “A thorn, and what is above it?” He said: “Then my father prayed for himself that the illness would not leave him until he died after not distracting him from Hajj, Umrah, or jihad in the path of God. “There is no prescribed prayer in congregation.” He said: “No man touched his skin after that except that he felt its heat until he died.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7854 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7855","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Rishdin informed me, about... Amr bin Al-Harith, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me that Abu Al-Khair told him that he heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him, he narrates on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There is not a day’s work that is not completed. When a believer falls ill, the angels say: Oh. Our Lord, Your servant is so-and-so whom You have imprisoned. Then the Almighty Lord says: Conclude for him according to his deeds, until he recovers or dies. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7855 - Rushdin Wah"
"7856","Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abdullah bin Najiya told us, Ubayd Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd told us, Aslam al-Kufi told me, on the authority of Murrat al-Tayyib, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: We were with Abu Bakr. Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, called for a drink and it was brought water and honey. When he brought it to his mouth, he cried and cried until his companions cried, but they remained silent, but he did not remain silent. Then he came back and cried until they thought they would not be able to ask him. He said: Then he wiped his eyes and they said: O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him. What made you cry? He said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him defending something from himself, but I did not see anyone with him, so I said: O Messenger of God, what are you defending? About yourself? He said: “This world appeared to me, so I said to it, ‘Away with me,’ then she came back and said, ‘If I escape from me, no one will escape from me after you.’” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7856 - Abd Al-Samad, left by Al-Bukhari and others"
"7857","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Qatada bin Al-Numan, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God loves a servant, he protects him in this world just as one of you protects his sick person with water.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7857 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7858","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Thabit bin Yazid told us, Hilal bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was on the Mat affected his side and he said: O Messenger of God, if you had a better bed than this, he said: “What do I have to do with this world? What does this world have to do with me?” By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of this world are nothing but like a rider who rode on a summer day and stayed in the shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then departed. “And he left it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. “And this is witnessed by the hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7858 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7859","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Once, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have nothing to do with this world. I am only like myself.” The example of this world is that of a rider who sat under a tree on a summer day and left it."
"7860","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz and Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Bandar Al-Zahid told us, saying: Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Al-Hasan informed us Al-Asqalani, Ibrahim bin Amr Al-Saskiki told us, Abi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever seeks what is with God, the sky will be his shade and the earth his bed. He will not care about anything.” The matter of the world, he does not plant crops while eating bread, and he does not plant trees and eat fruits out of trust in God Almighty and seeking To please Him, so God has guaranteed the seven heavens and the seven earths His provision. They labor over it and bring it lawful, and He completes His provision without anything else. An account with God Almighty until certainty comes to him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration for the Syrians, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7860 - Rather, it is objectionable or fabricated"
"7861","Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan told us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Shurayh Ibn Ubaid, that Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, when death approached him, said: O community of Ash’aris, let the witness be informed. Among you who is absent is that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The bitterness of this world is the bitterness of the hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7861 - True"
"7862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Al-Khorasani, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Give glad tidings to this nation of prosperity, exaltation, victory, and empowerment on earth, and whoever among them does the work of the Hereafter for this world will not have it in it.” The Hereafter is a share.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7862 - True"
"7863","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far al-Warkani told me, Adi bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {So whomever God wishes to guide, He will open his chest to Islam} [Al-An’am: 125] So the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When light enters the chest, it is revealed.” It was said: O Messenger of God, does this have any knowledge that can be known? He said: “Yes, avoiding the abode of deception, turning to the abode of eternity, and preparing for death before it descends.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7863 - Adi bin Al-Fadl has fallen"
"7864","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Juwayriyah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Four things are not afflicted except with astonishment: silence.” It is the beginning of worship, humility, remembrance of God Almighty, and the lack of something.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n Fahd bin Awf, Omar bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Raqaba bin Masqala, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, he said: I ate meat A lot and a lot of porridge. Then I came and sat next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I burped. He said: “Short your belches, for most people are full.” In this world, the hungriest are the ones in the hereafter.” True."
"7865","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amrwayh Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa told us Al-Ashayb, Uqba bin Abdullah Al-Asam told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “When a man says to a hypocrite, ‘O my master, he has angered his Lord, Blessed and Most High.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7865 - Uqba bin Al-Asam is weak"
"7866","Ahmad ibn Abi Uthman al-Zahid told me, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib told me, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith told me, My father, Harith bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The son of Adam has no right to anything except these qualities: a house to cover him, a garment to cover his private parts, and a sack of bread and water.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7866 - True"
"7867","Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Khalidi told us, Abu al-Abbas told us, on the authority of Masruq, Shurayh bin Yunus told us, Sa`id bin Muhammad al-Warraq told us, Salih bin Hassan, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Aisha, if... You want to join me, so let this world be enough for you like a rider’s provisions. Do not make a garment until you patch it, and beware of sitting with the rich.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7868","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Ishaq bin Nasih told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Tariq, prepare for death.” “Before the descent of death” is true.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7868 - True"
"7869","Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave income to the rich, for it is possible that you do not despise The blessings of God Almighty. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7869 - True"
"7870","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ja’far bin Abi Othman Al-Tayalisi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Wahb told us, Saad bin Tariq reported on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The blessings of the worldly abode are for those who provide From it to his hereafter until his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, is satisfied. And wretched is the abode for he who turns him away from his hereafter and falls short of his Lord’s satisfaction, and when The servant said, “God is disgraceful to the world.” The world said, “God is disgraceful to those who disobey their Lord.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7870 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"7871","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Hafiz told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Ufair ibn Ma`dan told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a servant becomes ill, God inspires His angels: O my angels, I have bound My servant with one of My fetters. If I seize him, I will forgive him, and if I pardon him, then he will sit and not commit any sin. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7871 - Afeer bin Ma’dan is weak"
"7872","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever dies doing something, God will resurrect him for it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7872 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7873","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja`far al-Aadmi al-Qari, in Baghdad, narrated to us, Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Nasih narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nasih narrated to us. Amr Al-Qurashi, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, advised a man He said: “Avoid the world and God Almighty will love you, and abstain from what is in the hands of people and the people will love you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7873 - Khalid bin Amr Al-Qurashi is lost"
"7874","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Ma’iz Al-Amiri, on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger God spoke to me about something that I should adhere to. He said: “Say, ‘My Lord is God, then be upright.’” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, how much do I fear for myself? He said: So he took his breath and then said: “This” is “a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7874 - True"
"7875","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ishaq bin Abdul-Wahid al-Qurashi told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Silah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “A look is one of Satan’s poisoned arrows. Whoever abandons it out of fear of God, the Almighty and Majestic, will reward him with faith that will find its sweetness in his heart.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7876","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Shuaib bin Yahya told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If you have four, it will not matter what you missed. “This world: keeping trustworthiness, truthfulness in speech, good character, and chaste food.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7876 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7877","Abu Hafs bin Omar bin Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Jumahi told us, in Mecca in the house of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Masry told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man did work in a rock that has no door or opening, his work would go out to the people in some form.” “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7877 - True"
"7878","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Al-Hakim bin Nafi told us, Ufayr bin Ma’dan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God Let one of you be tested by calamity even though he knows it, just as one of you tests his gold in fire. Among them are some, and it comes out as fine gold. This is the one whom God Almighty has saved from evil deeds, and among them are those who come out as gold, other than that. This is the one who has some doubt, and among them are those who “It will come out like black gold. This is the one who was tempted.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not bring it out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7878 - True"
"7879","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya Al-Qurashi told us, Ishaq bin Ka’b told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The affliction continues “With the believer in his body and his property until he meets God Almighty, and there is no sin upon him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7879 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7880","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: Abdullah said: “You pray more and fast more than The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they were better than you. They said: And with what? He said: “They were more ascetic than you in this world and more desirous of the Hereafter than you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7880 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7881","Abu Al-Nadr, the jurist, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth told us, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me that Ali bin Rabah told him that he heard Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, say on the pulpit: “By God I have never seen a people who desired what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, abstained from. You desire the world and he abstained from it. By God, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not pass by the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for three years except that what he owed was greater than what he owed.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. Al-Bukhari and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7881 - True"
"7882","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, my grandfather told us, Sa’id bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah told me Ibn Junada Al-Maafiri, that Abu Abdul-Rahman Al-Hubali told him, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The world is the believer’s prison and its Sunnah. So when he leaves the world, he leaves the prison and its Sunnah.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7882 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7883","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu al-Fadl Muhammad bin al-Hussein al-Qattan told me, Muhammad bin Muqatil al-Marwazi told us, Yusuf told us Ibn Atiyya, who was one of the Sunnis, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It will happen at the end of Time is ignorant worshipers and immoral reciters.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7883 - Yusuf bin Attiyah perished"
"7884","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf Al-Tai told us, Al-Mughirah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam told us, Damra told us Ibn Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God loves every sad heart.” This hadith The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7884 - Interrupted"
"7885","Ali bin Bandar al-Zahid told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Sulayman bin Yusuf al-Sulaiti told us, Ali bin Saeed al-Nasawi told us, Abd al-Samad told us Ibn Abdullah Al-Warith, Hashim bin Saeed Al-Kufi told us, Zaid bin Abdullah Al-Khathami told us, on the authority of Asma bint Umays Al-Khatha’miyyah, Radi On her authority, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Wretched is the servant, a servant who imagined and was arrogant and forgot the great and sublime. The servant is a servant who was careless and indifferent to her and forgot the beginning and the end. Wretched is the servant. He is an oppressive and oppressive servant and forgets the graves and calamities. Wretched is the servant. He who distorts the world with religion. A wretched servant is a servant who distorts religion with doubts. A wretched servant is a servant whose fear turns him away from the truth. A wretched servant is a servant. Greed guides him, miserable is the servant who leads him astray.” This is a hadith in which there is no one attributed to any kind of injury in its chain of transmission. And if that is the case “It is true and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7885 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"7886","Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, and Ali bin Hamshadh al-Adl told us, saying: Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abu Uwais, Suleiman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Jamil, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let them be picked just as dates are picked from a bunch. Let the best of you go and let the worst of you remain. So die if “You were able.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. And Abu Jamil is Al-Ta’i.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7886 - True"
"7887","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Musa bin Khalaf Al-Rasaghi told us, Abu Farwa Yazid bin Muhammad Al-Rahawi, my father told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of Bilal, may God be pleased with them both, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O Bilal, meet God as a poor person and do not meet him as a rich one.” He said: I said: How can I do that, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “If you are provided with provision, do not hide it, and if you are asked, do not withhold.” He said: I said: How can I do that, O Messenger of God? He said: “That is it, otherwise the Fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7887 - Wow"
"7888","Da'laj ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abar told us, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told us, Ja`far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Mecca with his chin on his mount, with his head humbled.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7888 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7889","Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Khalidi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Qattan told us, Ismail bin Al-Attar told us, Ishaq bin Bishr told us, Sufyan told us Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever wakes up in the morning with this world His greatest concern is not from God in anything, and whoever does not fear God is not from God in anything, and whoever does not care about Muslims in general is not from them.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7889 - I consider the news fabricated"
"7890","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Shababah bin Siwar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Israel, On the authority of Ja`dah al-Jashmi, may God be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, pointing with his hand to the belly of a fat man and saying: “If only this “Other than this, it would have been better for you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7890 - True"
"7891","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of his sheikhs, he said: Saad came to see Salman and visit him. He said: He cried, and Saad said to him: What makes you cry, Abu Abd? God? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and he was satisfied with you, and you went to him at the Basin and met your companions. He said: Salman said: As for me, I do not cry. Out of fear of death and not out of concern for the world, but the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a covenant with us in life and in death. He said: “Let it be in a language “Is there any of you in this world like the provision of a rider?” And around these blacks, he said: “Nearly around him is a shield, a veil, and a purifier.”\nSo Saad said to him: O Abu Abdullah, have you entrusted us with a covenant that we will follow after you? He said: So he said: “O Saad, remember God when you worry, when you decide, and when you decide, when you judge.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7891 - True"
"7892","Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastawayh told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Amr bin Uthman bin Aws Al-Wasiti told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ bin Umaylah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No one commits a large amount of usury but the consequences of his affair will be small.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7892 - True"
"7893","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Burd al-Antaki told us, Muhammad ibn Issa ibn al-Tabba’ told us, Muhammad ibn Issa ibn al-Tabba’ told us Abu Muawiyah, Abdullah bin Maimun told us, on the authority of Musa bin Miskin, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: “Whoever slanders a Muslim with a word that unjustly disgraces him, God will disgrace him with it in Hell on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7893 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"7894","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubayra, on the authority of Abu Tamim Al-Jishani, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you had put your trust in God as He deserves, He would have provided for you as He provides for the birds. “And you leave quietly.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7894 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7895","Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Qari told us, my uncle Muhammad bin Al-Ashras Al-Sulami told me, Abd al-Samad bin Hassan told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri, Abu Salamah Al-Khurasani told me, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give good tidings to my nation of prosperity, exaltation, and empowerment in the country as long as they do not seek this world by doing the work of the hereafter. He who seeks this world by doing the work of the Hereafter will have no share in the Hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"7896","Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Ismail told us, the merchant in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abu Salih told us, Muawiyah told us Ibn Salih, that Abd al-Rahman Ibn Jubayr Ibn Nufayr told him on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka`b Ibn Iyadh, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Indeed, every nation has a trial, and the trial of my nation is money.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7896 - True"
"7897","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Abu Muammar told us, Ismail bin Jafar told us, on the authority of Amr, Mawla al-Muttalib, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Hantab, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever loves This world is harmed by his hereafter, and whoever loves his hereafter is harmed by his worldly life, so prefer what endures over what perishes.” This is an authentic hadith.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7897 - True"
"7898","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Mahmoud Al-Muqri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Saad told us, Amr bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Al-Mustarid, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. So they remembered this world and the Hereafter, and some of them said: “Indeed, this world is a harbinger of the Hereafter. In it is work, and in it is prayer, and in it is zakat. A group of them said: In the Hereafter is Paradise, and they said, “Whatever God wills.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The world in the Hereafter is nothing but “Just as one of you walks to the sea and inserts his finger into it, and whatever comes out of it is the world.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7898 - True"
"7899","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Abu Aqeel told us Abdullah bin Aqeel Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, and Atiya bin Qais, on the authority of Atiya bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, and he was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man is not among the pious until he abandons what is harmless out of caution for what is harmless.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7899 - True"
"7900","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Yahya bin Ayoub, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him On their authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The believer’s masterpiece is death.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7900 - Ibn Ziyad is the African weak"
"7901","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told me, Yahya bin Bishr Al-Jariri told us, Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Qalaba told me that Abd al-Rahman bin Shaybah told him that the Mother of the Believers Aisha May God be pleased with her. She told him that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, the righteous will be emphasized.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7901 - True"
"7902","Abdul-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz told us, in Baghdad, Ubayd Allah bin Ahmad bin al-Hasan al-Maruzi told us, Ishaq bin Bishr told us, Muqatil bin Sulayman, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever becomes concerned with other than God is not of God in anything, and whoever does not care about the Muslims is not of them.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7902 - Ishaq and Muqatil are neither trustworthy nor truthful"
"7903","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad bin Abbas, on the authority of his brother Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “And such is sincerity” - he gestured with his finger next to the thumb - “and this is supplication” - so he raised his hands to the level of his shoulders - And this supplication - he raised his hands outstretching - “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7903 - This is a complete disgrace"
"7904","Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Simsar Al-Warraq told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad Al-Aishi told us, Hammad told us Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty He made the whole world a little, and what remains of it is only a little, and the likeness of what remains of it is like a hole - meaning a stream - the purest of which has been drunk. “And his dirt remained.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7904 - True"
"7905","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Yazid ibn Khumayr, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Marthad, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If you only knew I do not know, you would have cried a lot and laughed a little, and you would have gone out to the ascents, running to God Almighty, not knowing whether you would be saved or not. “You will be saved.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7905 - True"
"7906","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Saeed. Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “None of you waits for anything but overwhelming wealth or poverty.” Forgotten, or a corrupting disease, or old age that will be destroyed, or inevitable death, or the Dajjal and the Antichrist, an absent and awaiting evil, or the Hour and the Hour is worse. “And I order,” Al-Hakim said: “If Muammar bin Rashid heard from Al-Maqbari, then the hadith is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7906 - If Muammar heard from Al-Maqbari, then it is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"7907","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, said: I heard Busr bin Ubaid Allah, saying: I heard Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, saying: I heard Al-Nawwas bin Simeon Al-Kalabi, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no heart except between two of the fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills, He can place it And if He wishes, He can cause it to change.”\nThe Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, O Turner of hearts, make our hearts firm on Your religion, and the scales are in the hand of the Most Gracious. people and will put others on hold until the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7907 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7908","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told us, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Siwar told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim al-Kufi told us, in Egypt, Hibban ibn Ali, on the authority of Saad bin Tarif, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Nabatah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Ali, seek kindness from the merciful people of my nation who live among them, and do not seek it from those whose hearts are hard, for the curse will descend upon them.”\n“O Ali, God Almighty created good deeds and created people for it, so He made it endearing to them, made its doers endear to them, and directed its seekers to them just as He directed “Water in the dry land, so that it may be given life and its people may be revived therewith.”\n“O Ali, the people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7909","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, Ahmad bin Ziyad bin Mihran told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, he informed us Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Increase “He mentioned death.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7909 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7910","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khurasani, Al-Adl, told us, Yahya bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr bin Atiya, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Saad bin Al-Ahram, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not take the estate for the sake of this world.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7910 - True"
"7911","Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qaari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abu Ayyub Sulayman bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Khalid bin Yazid bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Malik Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, give me life as a poor person, and cause me to die as a poor person, and gather me in the group of the poor. “And the most wretched of the wretched is he who is combined with the poverty of this world and the torment of the hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7911 - True"
"7912","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, on the authority of Amr ibn Haritha, on the authority of Abu Umayyah al-Sha’bani, he said: I asked Abu Tha’labah about this verse {O O you who have believed, yourselves are yours. The one who goes astray will not harm you if you are guided.} [Al-Ma’idah: 105] Then Abu Tha’labah said: You asked about her. As an expert, I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her before, and he said: “O Abu Tha’labah, enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong. So if you see miserliness obeyed, whims followed, and this world desired, and you see something that you must ask for, then you should blame yourself and leave them and the common people. Behind you are days of patience. Patience in them is like holding onto hot coals. The one who works in them will receive the reward of fifty for doing the same as his work. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7912 - True"
"7913","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Abi Issa Al-Hilali told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Hammam bin Yahya, Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. While he was reciting: Overcrowding distracted you to the point that you visited the graves. He said: “The son of Adam says: My wealth is mine, and do you get any of your wealth except what you wear, and you did well?” Or you ate and you spent, or you gave in charity and you spent. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7913 - True"
"7914","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Jarir bin Uthman told us, Abdul Rahman bin Maysara, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Bishr bin Jahash al-Qurashi, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spit on his palm. Then he placed his finger on it, then said: “God, Blessed and Most High, says: O son of Adam, you fail me, and I created you like this, so that when I made you equal and made you equal, you walked, you gathered, you withheld, until when you reached your throats, you said: Should I give in charity? When is the time for charity? “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and there is no He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7914 - True"
"7915","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah bin Muhammad Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yahya bin Bukair told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Aban bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sabah bin Muharib, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him On his authority, the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Be ashamed before God as you should be.” So we said: O Prophet of God, indeed we should be ashamed. He said: “Not that.” But whoever is truly ashamed before God, let him guard the head and what it contains, and the stomach and what it contains, and let him remember death and calamity, and whoever will. “He left the adornments of this world, and whoever does that has become truly ashamed before God.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7915 - True"
"7916","Ali bin Bandar Al-Zahid told me, Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told me, Ahmad bin Bakr Al-Balsi told me, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Sufyan told us Al-Thawri, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “A time will come upon the people when they will gather together in their mosques, and their only concern will be the world. God will have no need for them, so do not sit with them.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7916 - True"
"7917","Muhammad bin Al-Mu'mil bin Al-Hussein told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha'arani told us, Al-Nufaili told us, Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, Bashir bin Zazan, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Hakam, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “The Hour has drawn near, and people will not increase in this world except in eagerness, and they will not increase in distance from God except in distance.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7917 - This is objectionable"
"7918","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told me, Musa bin Harun told us, Abu Muammar Ismail bin Ibrahim al-Hudhali told us, Abu Osama, Kulthum bin Jabr told us, Sulayman bin Habib Al-Muharbi told us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, saying: “When The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent. His soldiers came to Satan and said: The Prophet of God has been sent and his nation has departed. Then Satan said: Do they love The world? They said: Yes. He said: If they love it, I do not care if they do not worship idols. They will not escape me, and I will attack them in the morning and go. With three things: taking money from what is not due to it, spending it in what is not due to it, and withholding it from what is due to it, and all evil is due to this. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7918 - Kulthum bin Jabr is weak"
"7919","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud Al-Zahid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Sahl bin Uthman told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about what most brings people into Paradise, and he said: “Piety and good morals.” He was asked about what most causes people to enter Hell, and he said: “The internal organs: the mouth and the private parts.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7919 - True"
"7920","Ahmad bin Sahl, the jurist in Bukhara, told us, Qais bin Unif told us, Qutaibah told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, Simak said: I heard Al-Nu’man, while he was on the pulpit, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, could not find anything to fill his stomach with.” “The young bird is hungry.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7920 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7921","Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Muddhikr Al-Razi told us, Abu Zar’ah Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Karim told us, Issa bin Subaih told us, Zafir bin Suleiman told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he once said: On the authority of Ibn Omar, and he once said: On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Muhammad, live as you wish, for you will die, and love whomever you love, for you will depart from him, and do whatever you wish.” For you will be rewarded for it.” Then he said: “O Muhammad, the honor of a believer is to pray the night prayers, and his dignity is his being independent of people.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, but it is known from the hadith of Muhammad bin Humayd, on the authority of Zafir, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah, on the authority of a trustworthy sheikh of doubt, and this narration on the authority of Sahl Ibn Saad, without a doubt about it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7921 - True"
"7922","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Salam bin Abi Muti’ told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Countiness is wealth and generosity is piety.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7922 - True"
"7923","Ali ibn Bandar al-Zahid told me, Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Abi Awn al-Nasawi told me, Muhammad ibn Abd Rabbuh Abu Tamila told us, Abu Tamailah told us Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “When the Muslims hated their scholars and showed off the construction of their markets and married each other to collect dirhams, God Almighty would throw them away.” With four characteristics: through drought due to time, injustice from the ruler, betrayal from the rulers, and disobedience from the enemy. “This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic if Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika heard from the Commander of the Faithful, peace be upon him.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7923 - Rather, it is an interrupted denial"
"7924","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdul Majeed bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawad told us, on the authority of His father, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O people, none of you will die until he has completed his livelihood, so do not delay provision and fear God, O people, and seek generously. “What was lawful and they left what was forbidden.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7924 - True"
"7925","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Haywa bin Shurayh Al-Hadrami told us, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, Yusuf bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Nuh bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ate coarse And he wore coarse clothes, he wore wool and shoes made of cloth. It was said to Al-Hasan: What is coarse? He said: “Barley is so thick that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to taste it except with a sip of water.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7925 - It is not valid"
"7926","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Hudhi told us, Salam bin Abi Muti’ told us, Muawiyah bin Qurrah narrated to us, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your Lord, Blessed, says: And God Almighty: O son of Adam, devote yourself to worshiping Me. I will fill your heart with wealth and fill your hands with sustenance. O son of Adam, do not distance yourself from Me, so I will fill your heart. Be poor and fill your hands with work. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7926 - True"
"7927","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us about Mecca, protected by God Almighty. Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Yazid Al-Muqri, Musa Ibn Ali Ibn Rabah told us, saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Amr Ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, saying, and he He addresses the people in Egypt: “How far is your guidance from the guidance of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for him, he was the most ascetic of people in this world. “You are the people who desire it the most.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7927 - True"
"7928","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Al-Hasan bin Ahmed bin Al-Layth told us, Amr bin Uthman Al-Siwaq told us, Abu Amer Al-Aqdi, Muhammad bin Abi Humaid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, advise me and concisely, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You must By despair of what is in the hands of people, and beware of greed, for it is present poverty, and perform your prayers while you are bidding farewell, and beware of what you excuse yourself from.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7928 - True"
"7929","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr, Al-Adl told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Abdullah bin Salih Al-Masry told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me that Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr told him on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He acknowledged that he said: “O Abu Dharr, do you think that an abundance of money is wealth?” I said: Yes. He said: “Do you think that lack of money is poverty?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “That is not so. Rather, wealth is the richness of the heart, and poverty is the poverty of the heart.”\nThen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked me about a man from the Quraysh, and he said: “How do you see him?” I said: If he asks, he is given, and if he is present, he enters. He said: Then he asked me about a man from the people of Suffah, and he said: “Do you know so-and-so?” I said: No, O Messenger of God. He said: He continued to sweeten it and describe it until I recognized it. He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “How do you see it?” I said: A poor man from the people of the mosque. He said: “It is better than the land’s growth like the other.” I said: O Messenger of God, should he not be given part of what is given to the other? He said: “If he is given, then it is his due, and if he is turned away, then he has been given a good deed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it with this. “Driving.” They only narrated it through Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Abu Dharr, briefly.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7929 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7930","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Abu Mushar told us, Sadaqa bin Khalid told me, he told me Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Urwa bin Muhammad bin Atiya told me, my father told me, that his father told him, he said: I came to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, among some of the Banu Sa’d bin Bakr. I was the youngest of the people, so they left me behind in their camps. Then they came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted them and fulfilled their needs, then he said: “Is there anyone of you left?” They said: Yes, a boy with us. We left him behind on our journey. So he ordered them to send for me, so they came to me and said: Answer the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I came to him, and when he saw me he said: “May God not enrich you, so do not ask people for anything, for the upper hand is the one that is extended and the lower hand is The one who is given, and indeed the wealth of God Almighty is responsible and given.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to me in our language. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7930 - True"
"7931","Amr bin Ismail bin Nujaid Al-Sulami told me, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Mu’affa bin Suleiman told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Abu Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab bin Bakht, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The heart of the sheikh is young to love two things: a long life and an abundance of money.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7931 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7932","Abu Bakr told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on many occasions. Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Muttalib Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My Lord, Ash’ath “The most dusty of Dhul-Tamrain that people’s eyes can ignore. If he had sworn an oath to God, he would have fulfilled it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. I think a Muslim narrated it from Hadith of Hafs bin Abdullah bin Anas \"\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7932 - True"
"7933","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid, Ayyash bin Abbas told me, on the authority of Issa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he went out to the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and found Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, at the grave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was crying, and he said: What makes you cry, Muadh? He said: Something I heard from the owner of this grave makes me cry. He said: What did I hear? He said: I heard him say: “The slightest bit of hypocrisy is polytheism, and whoever is hostile to God’s friend has fought against God Almighty, and God loves The hidden pious ones, who, if they were absent, would not be missed, and if they were present, they would not be called upon, nor would their hearts be known. They are the lamps of guidance, coming out of every world. \"This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7933 - True"
"7934","Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih and Abu Amr ibn Sabir al-Bukhari told me, saying: Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz told us, Sa`id ibn Suleiman, Abu Aqeel Yahya bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, Omar bin Muhammad Al-Amri told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever makes concerns one concern, God will suffice him for what concerns him regarding the affairs of this world and the hereafter, and whoever has them intertwined.” Concerns: God does not care in which valley of the world he perishes. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7934 - Yahya bin Al-Mutawakkil is weak"
"7935","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya Al-Qurashi told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The heart of the son of Adam is like a bird, it turns over and over. “Seven times today.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7935 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary in this place, and he preceded it with No. 7850 and said there: There is a break in it."
"7936","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Khaled bin Khadash Al-Azdi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us Wahb, Amr ibn al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj Abi al-Samh, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Rabih ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Hidden polytheism is when a man does “For the place of a man.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7936 - True"
"7937","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ubaid bin Sharik told me, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told me, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, Amara bin Ghaziyeh, Ya’la bin Shaddad bin Aws told me, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: “We used to count during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7937 - True"
"7938","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad, the jurist in irrigation, narrated the hadith to us on its face, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris narrated to us, Affan narrated to us. Ibn Muslim, Abdul-Hamid Ibn Bahram told us, Shahr Ibn Hawshab told us, Abd al-Rahman Ibn Ghanam told us, on the authority of Shaddad Ibn Aws Radi On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Whoever prays while seeing himself has committed polytheism, and whoever fasts while watching has committed polytheism. And whoever gives charity while he is showing off has committed polytheism.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7938 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7939","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Muammar informed, about... Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Tawus, said: A man said: “O Prophet of God, I stand in positions seeking the face of God and I love for him to see my homeland.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond to him until the verse “So whoever hopes to meet his Lord, let him do righteous deeds” was revealed [Al-Kahf: 110].”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7939 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7940","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Zaid, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, said: I entered upon Shaddad bin Aws, may God be pleased with him, in his place of prayer and he was crying, so I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman What made you cry? He said: A hadith I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: What is it? He said: While I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I saw something on his face that upset me, so I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, O Messenger of God. What happened? Do I see your face? He said: “It is something that I fear for my nation after me.” I said: What is it? He said: “polytheism and a hidden desire.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, will you associate your nation with others after you? He said: “O Shaddad, they do not worship the sun, the moon, an idol, or a stone, but they show off to people by their deeds.” I said: O Messenger of God, Is hypocrisy a trap? He said: “Yes.” I said: What is hidden desire? He said: “One of you fasts in the morning and a worldly desire appears to him, so he breaks his fast.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7940 - Abd al-Wahid bin Zaid is abandoned"
"7941","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani informed me, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim al-Ghafari told us, Musa bin Dawud al-Dhabi told us, Ya`qub told us Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said to me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Visit the graves and remember the hereafter, and wash the dead, for treating an empty body is an eloquent admonition, and pray Concerning funerals. Perhaps that will make you sad, for the sad person will be in the shadow of God on the Day of Resurrection. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7941 - True"
"7942","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Ahmad ibn Bashir ibn Saad al-Murtadi told me, Yahya ibn Mu’in told me, Yahya ibn Mu’in told me. Hisham bin Yusuf, Abdullah bin Buhair told us, saying: I heard Hani, the servant of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, saying: I saw Uthman, He was standing on a grave and weeping until his beard was wet. Then it was said to him: Do you remember Paradise and Hell and do not weep and cry over this? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The grave is the first stage of the Hereafter, so if one escapes from it, then what comes after it is easier than it, even if not.” He will be saved from it, for what comes after it is worse than it.”\nI heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “I have never seen a sight except that the grave was more horrific than it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7942 - True"
"7943","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Yazid, the academic reader, told us in Baghdad. Abu Ja’far Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Nasih the grammarian told us, Muhammad bin Musab Al-Qurqasa’i told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Awza’i told me, Makhoul told me, on the authority of Ziyad bin Haritha, on the authority of Habib Ibn Maslamah, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for retaliation against himself for an insult committed by a Bedouin who did not baptizing him, so Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him and said: O Muhammad, God did not send you tyrannical or arrogant, so he called upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Bedouin said: “Take revenge on me.” The Bedouin said: “I have made you and my mother as free as my father, and I would never have done that even if you came to me.” Myself, so he prayed for his well-being. Al-Hakim said: “Ahmad ibn Ubaid alone narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Mus’ab, and Muhammad ibn Mus’ab is trustworthy.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7943 - Ibn Adi Ahmad ibn Ubaid Saduq said: He has evil deeds, and Muhammad is weak."
"7944","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan told us, Hammam told us, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dhar, may God be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: I love you, Ahl al-Bayt, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “God,” he said: God, he said: “Then prepare a drought for poverty, for poverty is quicker to reach those who love us than the torrent from the top of the hill.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7944 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7945","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf told us, Abu Al-Mughirah told us, Sulayman bin Sulaym Abu Salamah Al-Kinani told us, Yahya bin Jabir Al-Tai told me, he said: I heard Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib Al-Kindi, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “No human being fills a vessel worse than his stomach. The son of Adam is sufficient for three meals to strengthen his loins. If it is inevitable, then a third of food “And a third for a drink and a third for himself.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7945 - True"
"7946","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Zahid told us, al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab told us, dictating from its ancient origin, and I asked him, Ali ibn told us. Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Madini, Yazid bin Harun told us, Azhar bin Sinan told Abu Khaled, a servant of Quraysh, he said: I heard Muhammad Ibn Wasi’ al-Azdi, he says: I entered upon Bilal ibn Abi Burdah ibn Abi Musa, and I said: O Bilal, your father told me on the authority of your grandfather, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In Hell there is a valley, and in the valley there is a well called ‘Hab, Hub’. It is God’s duty that every mighty man should dwell in it. “So fear God and do not dwell in it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7946 - True"
"7947","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Marwazi told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Omar bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Riyahi told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Love the poor and those who are with them, and love the Arabs from your heart, and ward off from the people what you know from your heart.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They brought it out if Omar Al-Rihihi heard from Hajjaj ibn Al-Aswad “the last book of Al-Riqaq”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7947 - True"
